course: dictionary
lesson: 11197
title: Withdrawal: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Withdrawal is one of them. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «He made a cash withdrawal at the bank» means he took money out of his account.
explain: The same word can also mean moving away from a place. «Strategic withdrawal» is the official way to say an army retreated, which means it moved back on purpose. The clue is the army and the place it left.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: what is being taken, moved or stopped? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Withdrawal is a noun: one withdrawal, many withdrawals.
fact: Withdrawal can mean taking money out of a bank account, as in «cash withdrawal». It can also mean taking something away or back, as in «the withdrawal of an offer».
fact: Withdrawal can mean moving soldiers or people back or away from a place, or stopping taking part, such as a player leaving a race.
fact: «Withdrawal symptoms» are the ill feelings a person may have when they stop taking a drug their body is used to.
fact: Withdrawal can also mean becoming quiet and not wanting to be with people.
exercise: «The bank charged a fee for the cash withdrawal.» What does withdrawal mean here? | Adding money into an account | Moving soldiers away from a town | Stopping a race | *Taking money out of an account
exercise: «The army's strategic withdrawal took place at night.» What does withdrawal mean here? | Winning a race | A big party | Taking money out of a bank | *A planned move back, away from a place
exercise: «Her withdrawal from the race surprised the crowd.» What does withdrawal mean here? | Running faster than everyone | Moving soldiers out of town | Taking money out | *Stopping taking part in the race
test: «After the withdrawal of the offer, nobody could buy the bike.» What does withdrawal mean here? | Adding a prize | Becoming quiet | *Taking something away or back
test: «After he stopped the drug, he had withdrawal symptoms for days.» What are withdrawal symptoms? | *Ill feelings when the body stops a drug it is used to | Symptoms of a cold | Feeling hungry after a long walk
exam: Which phrase means taking money out of a bank account? | withdrawal symptoms | *cash withdrawal | strategic withdrawal | withdrawal from the race
